  "mn85:58.1": "<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Padhāna</i> is literally to “fix” or “place” and hence to “try” or “strive”. Its core application is to apply oneself to spiritual practices, and hence in Buddhism it overlaps in meaning with “meditation”; a <i lang='pi' translate='no'>padhānasāla</i> is a “meditation hall”. Here the five factors are qualities that are essential foundations for meditation. ",
