  "mn85:61.6": "His “lady mother” (<i lang='pi' translate='no'>ayyā</i>), as noted above, was Queen Vāsuladattā, daughter of Pajjota and wife of Udena. | This is the only place in the Pali canon where the idiom “heard and learned this in the presence” is applied to anyone other than the Buddha. ",
